  "query_preview": "..\n\nKEY MESSAGES:\n\n- Patchy fog and low stratus the next couple of morning.\n\n- Return of active weather for much of next week. \n\n\nThe widespread precipitation from yesterday along with clearing\nskies is allowing for the development of patchy fog and low\nstratus across the Northern Rockies this morning. The region\nshould anticipate fog and stratus the next couple of mornings as a\nweak ridge of high pressure will be over the region. \n\nMultiple low pressure systems are expected to swing into the\nPacific Northwest and the Northern Rockies starting late Monday\nthrough much of next week. These disturbances will bring periods\nof widespread precipitation with at times accumulating snow in the\nhigher terrain. Temperatures throughout the period appear to\nremain near seasonal averages of afternoon highs in the 40s and\n50s.",
